From: TB710FU clean board
Subject: [PATCH] Map the diagnostic segment RX before the TTBR1 switch

Diagnostic hook, a no-op unless the loaded kernel really has the segment.

The early-reporter diagnostic appends a __KDIAG segment past __BOOTDATA, in the
gap between __BOOTDATA and dynamic_memory_begin. arm_vm_prot_init() maps the
named segments and the derived ranges it knows about, and nothing covers that
gap. Once arm_vm_init() calls set_mmu_ttb_alternate() the segment therefore has
no translation, and entering it takes an instruction abort at its first byte.

That is why every earlier probe could show at most
"XNU enter: vm/set_mmu_ttb_alternate#1" and then nothing: the reporter had
already run out of reachable code, and the last visible line was a reporting
boundary rather than the fault PC.

This maps __KDIAG RX alongside the other read-only-executable mappings, all of
which run before the switch. The lookup is unconditional on purpose: an earlier
revision gated it on a tb-diag-segment boot argument, the compiled gate was
correct (it branches on the parse result), but the argument never reached the
kernel on this board, so the mapping silently never happened. Selecting the
segment by name removes that entire failure mode.

Nothing is mapped unless the segment exists: getsegdatafromheader() returns NULL
and sets size 0 for an unknown name, and the block requires both to be non-zero.
A kernel without the diagnostic segment therefore behaves exactly as before.

Not a functional fix. It exists so the reporter can keep drawing past the TTBR1
switch on a board that has no console and no working pstore.
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
--- a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
@@ -1801,7 +1801,31 @@ arm_vm_prot_init(__unused boot_args * args)
 	if (segLASTDATACONSTB) {
 		arm_vm_page_granular_RWNX(segLASTDATACONSTB, segSizeLASTDATACONST, ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_BLOCK); // __LASTDATA_CONST may be empty, but we cannot assume this
 	}
 	arm_vm_page_granular_RWNX(segPRELINKDATAB, segSizePRELINKDATA, ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_BLOCK | ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_HINT); // Prelink __DATA for kexts (RW data)
+
+	/*
+	 * TB710FU diagnostics: map the appended diagnostic segment RX.
+	 *
+	 * The reporter lives past __BOOTDATA, in the gap between __BOOTDATA and
+	 * dynamic_memory_begin. No mapping above covers it, so once arm_vm_init()
+	 * switches TTBR1 the reporter cannot draw again and every earlier probe
+	 * ended at set_mmu_ttb_alternate#1 regardless of where the kernel really
+	 * stopped. Mapping it here - before the switch - keeps the reporter
+	 * reachable so its output shows how far execution actually gets.
+	 *
+	 * Keyed on the segment name only, with no boot argument: a kernel built
+	 * without the diagnostic segment has no such segment, the lookup returns
+	 * null with size zero, and nothing is mapped.
+	 */
+	{
+		unsigned long diag_size = 0;
+		vm_offset_t diag_base = (vm_offset_t)getsegdatafromheader(
+		    &_mh_execute_header, "__KDIAG", &diag_size);
+		if (diag_base && diag_size) {
+			arm_vm_page_granular_ROX(diag_base, diag_size, 0,
+			    ARM64_PAGE_UNGUARDED);
+		}
+	}
 
 	if (segSizePLKLLVMCOV > 0) {
 		arm_vm_page_granular_RWNX(segPLKLLVMCOVB, segSizePLKLLVMCOV, ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_BLOCK | ARM64_GRANULE_ALLOW_HINT); // LLVM code coverage data
